<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muhammad ibn Yahya Hamid al-Din</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1904</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as al-Mansur Muhammad</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muhammad ibn Yahya Hamid al-Din, who ruled as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">Imam</a> al-Mansur Muhammad, was the Zaydi imam of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a> from 1890 to 1904 and the founder of the Hamid al-Din dynasty. He led repeated risings against Ottoman rule in the highlands, including sieges of Sanaa, and his resistance was continued by his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yahya-muhammad-hamid-ed-din">Imam Yahya</a>, who later founded the Mutawakkilite Kingdom of Yemen.</p></div>
